{"title":"1966 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the lengths of the sides of a triangle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f03534a4415725670716640ebe03fd2fed3a3bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> respectively, the angles opposite these sides. Prove that if\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f9da0ef99a782cf1d2ceeb3677e43267397d825.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a+b=\\tan{\\frac{\\gamma}{2}}(a\\tan{\\alpha}+b\\tan{\\beta}),\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>the triangle is isosceles.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We'll prove that the triangle is isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\nWe'll prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Assume by way of contradiction WLOG that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.\nFirst notice that as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84ecbc61f2bfbce167b3919d4a9e22796d162be4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma = \\pi -\\alpha-\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> then and the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/634c1dfe87fd617caa36628868a5119ea7263c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan\\left(\\frac \\pi 2 - x \\right)=\\cot x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"162\" height=\"35\" /> our equation becomes:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1c3a6e7ad9660df3cdb00e2a28d476ff3586e9c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a+b=\\cot \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2}\\left(a\\tan \\alpha + b\\tan \\beta \\right)\\]\" width=\"282\" height=\"38\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd278cc330f9bafbb88664474be840209a38ddeb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff a\\tan\\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2}+b\\tan \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2}=a\\tan \\alpha + b\\tan \\beta\\]\" width=\"396\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1ea2bfcbcc0c9063ccf226363be2bbd7a3bb5ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff a\\left(\\tan \\alpha -\\tan \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2}\\right)+b\\left(\\tan \\beta -\\tan \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2}  \\right)=0\\]\" width=\"456\" height=\"43\" />\nUsing the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af46f944fdfe737034fa672a96678e9e6bf0edd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan (A-B)=\\frac {\\tan A-\\tan B}{1+\\tan A\\tan B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"242\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83f116b2d9cfc3be0b86ad61f553c00d1e26b2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\iff \\tan A-\\tan B=\\tan(A-B)(1+\\tan A\\tan B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"410\" height=\"20\" />\nand inserting this into the above equation we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e104076d54e67e960085ca32e1f1fa83cb12c026.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff a\\tan \\frac{\\alpha -\\beta}{2}\\left(1+\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2}\\right)+b\\tan \\frac{\\beta -\\alpha}{2}\\left(1+\\tan \\beta \\tan \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2} \\right)=0\\]\" width=\"635\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/414db68e49ff4c3e28eb2ad327d0ec02bfeaa3da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\underbrace{\\iff}_{\\tan -A=-\\tan A}a\\tan \\frac{\\alpha -\\beta}{2}\\left(1+\\tan \\alpha \\tan \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2}\\right)-b\\tan \\frac{\\alpha -\\beta}{2}\\left(1+\\tan \\beta \\tan \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2} \\right)=0\\]\" width=\"691\" height=\"49\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/5/8353f65dee16d3a0cd3caad6b565e0c0293d54b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff \\tan \\frac{\\alpha -\\beta}{2}\\left(a-b+\\tan \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2}(a\\tan\\alpha -b\\tan \\beta) \\right)=0\\]\" width=\"464\" height=\"43\" />\nNow, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and the definitions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/b/c7bd39c01460af94d001595c9370a6fa7a7c50fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,\\alpha,\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> being part of the definition of a triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415261166f0beb4495c99d91210eefebd25bf7e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha &gt;\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />.\nNow, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f88bf8d7891fd9c5c32a189122c9c8ac928e273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi &gt;\\alpha -\\beta &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b46c05ee88a803ee8fde67026cba275dc39dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha+\\beta +\\gamma = \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> and the angles are positive), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98a9eb1a8a48ba45a791efad6c41e8e5245c7de3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\frac{\\alpha -\\beta}{2}\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"39\" />, and furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154ec420e1a6b75c595d076884e6e27b6a84556d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{2}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"39\" />. By all the above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe8ddf3fb8a97b25b77bc52f2ddb140f21ae5f4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(a-b+\\tan \\frac{\\alpha +\\beta}{2}(a\\tan\\alpha -b\\tan \\beta) \\right)&gt;0\\]\" width=\"337\" height=\"43\" />\nWhich contradicts our assumption, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07c4ec907e9eec287e289f40ed55d577b19bca59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\leq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. By the symmetry of the condition, using the same arguments, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d997b30f7f09d32954c9b09f04a6599729dd6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we'll prove that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> are acute.\nAt least one of them has to be acute because these are angles\nof a triangle.  We can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is acute.  We want\nto show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> is acute as well.  For a proof by\ncontradiction, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caab991af60361d60ec4fdf12a66e818c86a138b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta \\ge \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>From the hypothesis, it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d053f9132a8f37c0338706629207eed26bed2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + b) \\tan \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} = a \\tan \\alpha + b \\tan \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"289\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317fc0ed4489071311173d3378b1b883a7b40bd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha &lt; \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\le \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"34\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  So,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da35c55acea248c482bae8b3d0a23c1fed82a3ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\tan \\beta = (a + b) \\tan \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} - a \\tan \\alpha &gt; 2a \\tan \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} - a \\tan \\alpha \\ge a (2 \\tan \\left( \\frac{\\alpha}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) - \\tan \\alpha) =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"735\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/1978857a3f04d2a29066227a380dfa10fcaf2b4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a \\left( \\frac{\\tan \\frac{\\alpha}{2} + 1}{1 - \\tan \\frac{\\alpha}{2}} - \\frac{\\tan \\frac{\\alpha}{2}}{1 - \\tan^2 \\frac{\\alpha}{2}} \\right) = 2a \\cdot \\frac{\\tan^2 \\frac{\\alpha}{2} + \\tan \\frac{\\alpha}{2} + 1} {1 - \\tan^2 \\frac{\\alpha}{2}} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"472\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>because the numerator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64a426abc13de68046197e4ef43028bcd6b09228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y^2 + Y + 1 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> for any real\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), and the denominator is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a9eb87a8534d62b2128c303d061ac64554d787d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha &lt; \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"33\" />,\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/9472844a60970a7826798833edc39f521bcba54c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\frac{\\alpha}{2} &lt; \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"149\" height=\"34\" />).\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/5497b00327a4f4d710079b4e3da75551293f7a44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\beta &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, so it can not be that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caab991af60361d60ec4fdf12a66e818c86a138b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta \\ge \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we will prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d053f9132a8f37c0338706629207eed26bed2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + b) \\tan \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} = a \\tan \\alpha + b \\tan \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"289\" height=\"39\" />\nimplies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb20e93132e1900f67863ab0cdbdb41e11be1cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbdff03fffbe5bd5ec4b00cff59af3c479b3affd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\sin \\alpha \\cdot 2R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26ad782f2bae45002b4f94e5dee49a82b7eaffe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\sin \\beta \\cdot 2R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />\n(in fact, we don't care that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the radius of the circumscribed\ncircle), and simplify by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e86afd07eb8be7351058918c6ecae8e9d6eccb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />.  We get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c1257408f620ddf66125186d81e3d7067de8bd0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sin \\alpha + \\sin \\beta) \\tan \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} = \\sin \\alpha \\tan \\alpha + \\sin \\beta \\tan \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"401\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>This becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a29236dcdc30f4068656edd8f8e5ba9500ff2f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\sin \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} \\tan \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} \\right) \\cdot \\cos \\frac{\\alpha - \\beta}{2} = \\frac{1}{2}(\\sin \\alpha \\tan \\alpha + \\sin \\beta \\tan \\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"509\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>We will show that the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46bcc45432bdef2724b89593264ae0d8165e294a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\tan x \\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" /> is convex on\nthe interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be406bca6effff3e21858787f3c45c3a88eb962f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 0, \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"35\" />.  Indeed, the first\nderivative is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7321bde81cff3f8e5ce4280726ef5f83dd394a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x) = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos^2 x} + \\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"173\" height=\"39\" />, and the\nsecond derivative is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c799488971fe39038a07b83c4de611929d2a1624.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;&#39;(x) = \\frac{\\cos^4 x - \\cos ^2 x + 2}{\\cos^3 x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"218\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e593e0181e9efb7f1e40f2353e57efcf9bb0bd5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;&#39;(x) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be406bca6effff3e21858787f3c45c3a88eb962f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 0, \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"35\" /> since the\nnumerator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f4896be0eb7510c45bf6bbc712b4e890cc63a04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y^2 - Y + 1 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> for any real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), and\nthe denominator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> on the interval\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be406bca6effff3e21858787f3c45c3a88eb962f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 0, \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"35\" />.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46bcc45432bdef2724b89593264ae0d8165e294a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\tan x \\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />\nis convex on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be406bca6effff3e21858787f3c45c3a88eb962f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 0, \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>Using the convexity we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76fe416a5f39573d806e689ff08b24df70012403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f \\left( \\frac{x + y}{2} \\right) \\le \\frac{1}{2} (f(x) + f(y))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"232\" height=\"45\" />.  In\nour case, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/6362f6df628f66040ef51335fb19f3e6387186b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(\\sin \\alpha \\tan \\alpha + \\sin \\beta \\tan \\beta) = \\left( \\sin \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} \\tan \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} \\right) \\cdot \\cos \\frac{\\alpha - \\beta}{2} \\le \\frac{1}{2}(\\sin \\alpha \\tan \\alpha + \\sin \\beta \\tan \\beta) \\cdot \\cos \\frac{\\alpha - \\beta}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"833\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>We can simplify by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/934d3a553685d98023b10b5c4c122c1518f433b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\alpha \\tan \\alpha + \\sin \\beta \\tan \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" />\nbecause it is positive (because both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/70023895dee56cef9e36a02cc119e0d61365da55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha, \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> are acute!),\nand we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/c/3dcd0bbbe5219ae12ee08d4e8faf15d1e9ad888a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le \\cos \\frac{\\alpha - \\beta}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"39\" />.  This is possible only when\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/34501cbfa73fd5e4dff92b1feb933d755997350c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\frac{\\alpha - \\beta}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"39\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb20e93132e1900f67863ab0cdbdb41e11be1cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, September 2024]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Here is a more natural and straightforward algebraic approach to this problem, without using contradiction or advanced calculus properties. \n</p><p>We are given:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4dfcc5fd61a20f935a3cc5b568ff5a8ec6c1a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + b = \\tan \\frac{\\gamma}{2} (a \\tan \\alpha + b \\tan \\beta)\\]\" width=\"247\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>First, multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42e4741fd5716e7649d77f35ab703420c9bd2767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cos\\frac{\\gamma}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"34\" /> to eliminate the half-angle tangent:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bcc7caff6a9ef97786500f9e56226719c542c259.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\cos\\frac{\\gamma}{2}(a + b) = 2\\sin\\frac{\\gamma}{2}(a \\tan \\alpha + b \\tan \\beta)\\]\" width=\"323\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Using the double-angle identity and substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3dbbaccad2655fc8e4c0cb4cabf91fc9c4ae1754.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\cos \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"39\" />, we can simplify the equation into:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9700ade786e2d9b5dee5d5e739c17ee6393a54df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\cos\\gamma + 1)(a + b) = \\sin\\gamma \\left( \\frac{a\\sin\\alpha}{\\cos\\alpha} + \\frac{b\\sin\\beta}{\\cos\\beta} \\right)\\]\" width=\"348\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>By the Law of Sines, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/83469221ac9b19f9e88a2248caf198e0fc91cdac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\alpha, \\sin\\beta, \\sin\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> are proportional to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Substituting these ratios and applying the Law of Cosines for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bb7c851fddc20825828d10aafc1560346b78b88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\alpha, \\cos\\beta, \\cos\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />, the equation transforms purely into side lengths:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cbaf104eda43cb0630f5ad335e2e48c54fb36592.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a+b}{c^2 - (a-b)^2} = \\frac{(a+b)(c^2 + a^2 - b^2)}{(b^2+c^2-a^2)(a^2+c^2-b^2)}\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd2f868a898bbce4b8c9cc87f06168d0bd88fb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />, we can cancel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be092b2283c00c376e719c5f650a15433d43a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> from both sides. Cross-multiplying and simplifying the polynomials yields a remarkably clean relation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/582150ff8d7f906af73efe36e21fb1e4fe1b4093.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b^2 + c^2 - a^2 = c^2 - a^2 + 2ab - b^2\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f5784af546fbf01a1b1069a5d28d1cd68d9c7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2b^2 = 2ab \\implies b(b-a) = 0\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> represents the side length of a triangle (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d09016ae7d4bb0ccd869b43b3da544e9bacc08e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />), we must have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef220c9aec64f58c725ba3f77e69829b424cd7a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = b\\]\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the triangle is isosceles. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By law of sines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17fcfc9853fb40b97a79217ae2cdb75aa1b801eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = a \\frac{\\sin \\beta}{\\sin \\alpha}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"39\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08fe14e3a107126d3aaebc2acbf8e9ce856b068b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\pi/2 - x) = \\cot x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />, and multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c695a9e1dbaa716f757bd8c00ab8abf8f2cee3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\alpha$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> gives \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/f/71f7ce4ca0c6e66599580f008d84bc5cedf27565.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin \\alpha + \\sin \\beta = \\cot \\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{2}\\Big(\\tan \\alpha \\sin \\alpha + \\tan \\beta \\sin \\beta \\Big). \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (1)\\]\" width=\"458\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b435360aabd12523b8c71f1dd062d7df68fab8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/b/d8b877292f7e63fbfc031ffeb275a12a036cd3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha,\\beta &lt; \\pi/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d89357bdd19795ccb9fd53b8528e215d4aa860c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x$\" width=\"39\" height=\"11\" /> is convex on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/67000e09b985dca1a74b8c9cb46e4ce50346ef21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pi/2), \\tan \\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{2} \\leq \\frac{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"279\" height=\"39\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b9afbe45738e77f03aaa986a811be9ac68304ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\text{RHS of } (1) &amp;\\geq \\frac{2}{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta} \\Big(\\tan \\alpha \\sin \\alpha + \\tan \\beta \\sin \\beta \\Big) \\\\                    &amp;=\\sin \\alpha \\frac{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta + \\tan \\alpha - \\tan \\beta}{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta} + \\sin \\beta \\frac{\\tan \\beta + \\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta - \\tan \\alpha}{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta} \\\\ &amp;= \\sin \\alpha + \\sin \\beta + \\frac{\\tan \\alpha - \\tan \\beta}{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta}(\\sin \\alpha - \\sin \\beta)  \\end{align*}\" width=\"667\" height=\"135\" />\nwhich is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3ed436172a450962d22cf060bfb90538c0f658f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\alpha + \\sin \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e3b1c3e0b3e60dc885515a83663053bf94104ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha \\neq \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b435360aabd12523b8c71f1dd062d7df68fab8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Case}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a6b29041a6f73994ad4f87a272c5d69a2b9546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{One of } \\alpha,\\beta &gt; \\pi/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />. Say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c51db3a84fbfe1e5644b7490d9c63bffa73b519c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta &gt; \\pi/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b0aa88c25ff32dc7f0ac8ea35183ed4aa7d58c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{2} &gt; \\tan \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"146\" height=\"39\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13fc7f0d87038b25797f839cf88f78e126df4a01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha &lt; \\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{2} &lt; \\pi/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"39\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> becomes \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15d27e29d3d4d542dc3eee14041d588813b566db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sin \\alpha + \\sin \\beta  &amp;&lt; \\cot \\alpha (\\sin \\alpha \\tan \\alpha + \\sin \\beta \\tan \\beta) \\\\             &amp;= \\sin \\alpha + \\sin \\beta \\frac{\\tan \\beta}{\\tan \\alpha} &lt; \\sin \\alpha  \\end{align*}\" width=\"354\" height=\"64\" />\nsince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c7b122863bd51db841e7584ca2a5c46de52260.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan \\beta &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/8/198c01e908c40b348f4e8c856b82120e35d7f4f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\alpha, \\beta \\neq 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO\" title=\"1966 IMO\">1966 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1966 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1966 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1966 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1966 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1966 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1966 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1966 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1966 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017004825\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.045 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 608/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 23871/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.362      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.362      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9727:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017004825 and revision id 291266. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}